@startuml 10_job_states
!pragma layout smetana
!include _style.iuml
title Background job lifecycle at the hub (jobs.status); the node has no queue (D53)
hide empty description

[*] --> QUEUED : enqueue\n(same transaction as the state change;\nunique dedupe_key blocks duplicates)

QUEUED --> RUNNING : worker claims\n(conditional UPDATE, run_after <= now)
RUNNING --> SUCCEEDED : handler finished
RUNNING --> QUEUED : error [attempts < max_attempts]\nrun_after = now + growing delay
RUNNING --> FAILED : error [attempts = max_attempts (3)]
RUNNING --> QUEUED : service startup:\nstuck job requeued

SUCCEEDED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note right of FAILED
  Hub ASSESS jobs: the assessment
  moves to FAILED; POST /retry
  enqueues a new job.
end note

note bottom of QUEUED
The queue exists only at the hub (no node <-> hub link).
  Hub kinds: NORMALIZE_ITEM | ASSESS | EXTRACT_ANSWERS |
  PROPOSE_ATTRIBUTE | SIMULATE_SUPPLIER | REBUILD_PROJECTION
  The node normalizes and rebuilds synchronously (D53).
end note

@enduml
